00:02:28.449 --> 00:02:38.449
So, and we can get back to this out because I like this too, but Craig, where did the idea for the opening credits This is kind of like friends, pictures, kind of popular.
所以，我们可以回到这个话题，因为我也喜欢这个，但是克雷格，片头的想法是从哪里来的？这有点像朋友、图片，很受欢迎。

00:02:38.449 --> 00:02:39.449
That was from the beginning.
从一开始就是如此。

00:02:39.449 --> 00:02:43.090
That was when we were writing the pilot, when the pilot got picked up.
那是我们在写试播集的时候，试播集被选中的时候。

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:44.689
We always had that idea.
我们一直有这个想法。

00:02:44.689 --> 00:02:47.169
This is a weird thing that I don't think I've ever talked about.
这是一件奇怪的事情，我想我从来没有谈论过。

00:02:47.169 --> 00:02:53.009
For a minute, I remember Carter Bay's, I think it might have been his concept to begin with.
有那么一瞬间，我想起了卡特·贝的想法，我想这可能是他最初的想法。

00:02:53.009 --> 00:02:58.810
And the way he wanted to do it at first was pictures of just young people in New York, not even our cast.
他一开始想要的只是纽约年轻人的照片，甚至不是我们的演员。

00:02:58.810 --> 00:03:02.770
This very abstracted idea of like, you're just seeing youth in New York.
这个非常抽象的想法，就像你在纽约看到的年轻人一样。

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:03.770
It could be anyone.
可以是任何人。

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:06.849
seeing this pastiche of New York City and people out.
看到纽约市和外面的人们的模仿。

00:03:06.849 --> 00:03:08.569
And it's just them and their friends, blah, blah, blah.
只有他们和他们的朋友，等等，等等。

00:03:08.569 --> 00:03:09.810
And I think we gained it out.
我认为我们已经成功了。

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.650
We started looking at it, we're like, this is too weird.
我们开始观察它，我们想，这太奇怪了。

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:12.490
Who are these people?
这些人是谁？

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:13.330
These aren't the same.
这些并不相同。

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:15.289
I mean, this is in the cast of the show.
我的意思是，这是节目的演员阵容。

00:03:15.289 --> 00:03:16.250
And that was how we learned.
这就是我们学习的方式。

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:18.729
I mean, it was sort of a little too artsy of an idea, maybe.
我的意思是，这个想法也许有点太艺术化了。

00:03:18.729 --> 00:03:21.090
And then we realized, let's get the cast to do this.
然后我们意识到，让演员们来做这件事吧。

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:24.689
But if I remember, currently, Josh, I think we did the pilot, right?
但如果我记得的话，乔什，我想我们现在已经完成了试播，对吧？

00:03:24.689 --> 00:03:25.969
We did a little photo shoot.
我们拍了一些照片。

00:03:25.969 --> 00:03:27.770
We did a photo shoot right away.
我们立即拍了一张照片。

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.409
Like in the booth, kind of like Candid's.
就像在展位上一样，有点像 Candid 的。

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:32.370
I remember, did Jason hold the camera?
我记得杰森拿着相机吗？

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.090
Was it like a selfie?
是不是像一张自拍照？

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:43.729
I think sometimes you guys were selfieing and I think sometimes literally Pam Fryman, our director, I think was like shooting it on at what at that time was like a crappy like disposable camera.
我想有时你们在自拍，有时我们的导演帕姆·弗莱曼(Pam ​​Fryman)，我认为就像用当时像一次性相机一样蹩脚的相机来拍摄。

00:03:43.729 --> 00:03:45.009
These were on phone packs, right?
这些是在手机包装上，对吗？

00:03:45.009 --> 00:03:52.129
And you see that Lily, it looks, and it dates the show so much, but you see in titles that Lily is holding that old disposable camera.
你看莉莉，它看起来，而且它与这部剧过时了很多，但你在标题中看到莉莉拿着那台旧的一次性相机。

00:03:52.129 --> 00:03:54.009
That's literally what they're still getting.
这确实是他们仍然得到的。

00:03:54.009 --> 00:03:57.289
So they're placed on tables at weddings, you know, there's still in use.
所以它们被放在婚礼的桌子上，你知道，它们仍然在使用。

00:03:57.289 --> 00:03:58.370
Ironically.
讽刺的是。

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:05.969
Where the like color scheme come up with like that kind of seepia, so I really like the kind of rods and yellows and.
类似的配色方案就像那种渗色，所以我真的很喜欢那种棒状和黄色。

00:04:05.969 --> 00:04:14.169
We said we wanted to feel like memories, like these sort of old tinge sort of like seepia tone, sort of like just this feeling of these exist as memories in someone's mind.
我们说我们想要感觉像回忆，就像这种古老的色调，有点像渗水的音调，有点像这些感觉作为记忆存在于某人的脑海中。

00:04:14.169 --> 00:04:15.490
Yeah.
是的。

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:16.329
Yeah.
是的。

00:04:16.329 --> 00:04:20.089
And when did you guys hit on using the solid song or the end of Hey Beautiful?
你们什么时候开始使用这首扎实的歌曲或《Hey Beautiful》的结尾？

00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:28.540
I think we, for a minute, we wanted to use, I've never said this either, I think, we wanted to use a replacement song.
我想我们，有一分钟，我们想使用，我也从来没有说过这个，我想，我们想使用一首替代歌曲。

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:33.696
The band replacement, Carter and I are huge fans replacements card turned me into a replacement span.
乐队的替换，卡特和我都是巨大的粉丝替换卡，把我变成了替换跨度。

00:04:33.696 --> 00:04:39.261
And we were talking about using, um, I think we're going to, I think we're going to use the song unsatisfied.
我们正在讨论使用，嗯，我想我们会，我想我们会不满意地使用这首歌。

00:04:39.261 --> 00:04:46.511
Like, and literally, I think we cut a version of the main titles that was pictures of total strangers set to the replacement song unsatisfied.
就像，从字面上看，我认为我们剪掉了一个主要标题的版本，该版本是完全陌生的照片，设置为替换歌曲不满意。

00:04:46.511 --> 00:04:51.003
It looks like it's just opening titles to an entirely different show called unsatisfied.
看起来这只是一个完全不同的节目《不满意》的开头。

00:04:51.003 --> 00:04:56.619
It was utterly confusing and it was a complete fail, but it's what taught us that we needed it to be our cast.
这完全令人困惑，而且完全失败，但它告诉我们，我们需要它作为我们的演员阵容。

00:04:56.619 --> 00:05:04.379
And the idea of photos and memories like that, that was always the idea, but we had to do a bad like misguided version of that to get to what it became.
像这样的照片和回忆的想法，这一直是我们的想法，但我们必须做一个像误导版本那样的坏事才能达到它的目的。

00:05:04.379 --> 00:05:08.540
And isn't Barney's last name after a guitar like a replacement?
巴尼的姓氏是不是就像吉他的替代品一样？

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:09.686
Yeah, Barney Stinson.
是的，巴尼·斯汀森。

00:05:09.686 --> 00:05:15.579
Stinson, Tommy Stinson is the bass player for the replacements, and that is a shout out to the replacements.
Stinson，汤米·斯廷森（Tommy Stinson）是替代者的贝斯手，这是对替代者的大声疾呼。

00:05:15.579 --> 00:05:22.459
Who again, and we really wanted to unsatisfied to be the song, and then we got the bill for what that would cost every week.
又是谁，我们真的很不满意成为这首歌，然后我们每周都会收到费用的账单。

00:05:23.339 --> 00:05:27.978
And then we said, what if we put our own band song on there, And we get that money.
然后我们说，如果我们把我们自己的乐队歌曲放在那里，我们就能得到这笔钱。

00:05:27.978 --> 00:05:30.773
And they said, what about one tenth of that money?
他们说，那十分之一的钱呢？

00:05:30.773 --> 00:05:31.500
I said souls.
我说灵魂。

00:05:33.819 --> 00:05:36.601
Craig, did you need to get approval at this point?
克雷格，此时你需要获得批准吗？

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:40.383
Did the studio or network have to like, look at that title sequence?
工作室或网络是否必须喜欢看那个标题序列？

00:05:40.383 --> 00:05:40.884
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

00:05:40.884 --> 00:05:41.385
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

00:05:41.385 --> 00:05:45.334
That thing is like tested and game down and sent up and down the chain.
那东西就像经过测试和游戏，并在链条上上下发送。

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:48.060
It's, it's, it's the branding of the show, right?
这是，这是，这是节目的品牌，对吧？

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:50.069
It's like the brand does become so iconic.
就好像这个品牌确实变得如此具有标志性。

00:05:50.069 --> 00:05:52.987
And what's amazing about it now is like, I see people online.
现在令人惊奇的是，我看到人们在线。

00:05:52.987 --> 00:06:02.220
I see people on socials like them and their friends are literally shot for shot recreating how I met your mother photos from the opening main titles and they're doing it with their own friends.
我看到像他们这样的社交媒体上的人和他们的朋友一起拍摄，重现我如何遇见你母亲的照片，他们是和自己的朋友一起做的。

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:08.800
And I find that so moving and pointing like we've passed this baton onto this younger generation who are now like enacting it.
我发现这非常令人感动和具有指向性，就像我们已经将接力棒传递给了年轻一代，他们现在正在执行它。

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:23.579
And it's their way of saying we're making our own memories now I think which is a story that Josh you've told to about a fan told you said do you I realize I'm living these memories now and that's I love the idea that like young people watching the show are creating that themselves.
这是他们说我们现在正在创造我们自己的回忆的方式，我想这是你给乔什讲过的一个关于粉丝告诉你的故事，你说我意识到我现在正在经历这些回忆，这就是我喜欢这样的想法，就像观看节目的年轻人正在创造自己的回忆一样。

00:06:23.579 --> 00:06:24.079
Yeah.
是的。

00:06:24.079 --> 00:06:25.747
So speaking of memories.
所以说到回忆。

00:06:25.747 --> 00:06:43.812
So Josh, so at this point when week three of producing this show, obviously spread over time between the pilot and the second episode, but what was your week like, at least in this first season, how did that script first come to on what day rehearsal blocking?
所以乔什，所以在制作这个节目的第三周，显然随着时间的推移在试播集和第二集之间传播，但是你的一周是什么样的，至少在第一季，这个剧本是如何在排练的哪一天第一次出现的？

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:45.502
How did it look for you?
你觉得怎么样？

00:06:45.502 --> 00:06:51.259
My memory is in Craig maybe like we would get an envelope over the weekend.
我的记忆在克雷格身上，也许我们周末会收到一个信封。

00:06:51.259 --> 00:07:02.006
Yeah, like on a Sunday, I think maybe sometimes Friday, sometimes Friday, but hard copies in a in a Manila envelope kind of like waiting at your door.
是的，就像周日一样，我想有时可能是周五，有时是周五，但硬拷贝装在马尼拉信封里，就像在你家门口等着一样。

00:07:02.006 --> 00:07:05.660
Yeah, and you'd read and that was the table script.
是的，您已经读过，这就是表格脚本。

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:09.759
That was the script we were going to read Monday at like 10 a.m.
这就是我们周一上午 10 点左右要读的剧本。

00:07:09.759 --> 00:07:10.272
Correct.
正确的。

00:07:10.272 --> 00:07:12.706
So the actors would come in at 10 a.m.
所以演员们会在上午 10 点进来。

00:07:12.706 --> 00:07:13.347
on Monday.
周一。

